## Why This Is Asked
Aimed to assess mastery of end-to-end guarantees across HTTP API, DB, Kafka, and Redis, including failure handling and read-model integrity.

## Key Concepts
- Outbox pattern
- Kafka transactional producers
- Idempotent consumers
- Cross-service failure handling
- Read model consistency and testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// PostgreSQL transaction: write user update and outbox row
BEGIN;
UPDATE users SET name = $1 WHERE id = $2;
INSERT INTO outbox (aggregate_type, aggregate_id, event_type, payload, sent)
VALUES ('user', $2, 'UserUpdated', '{id:' + $2 + ',name:' + $1 + '}', false);
COMMIT;
```

```javascript
// Pseudo publisher
async function publishOutbox() {
  const rows = await fetchUnsentOutbox();
  const txn = await kafka.beginTransaction();
  for (const r of rows) {
    await kafka.send({ topic: 'user.events', key: r.aggregate_id, value: r.payload }, txn);
  }
  await markOutboxSent(rows.map(r => r.id));
  await txn.commit();
}
```

